From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:42:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] docs: two decisions the shell and the board depend on

ADR-0027 records what the portal shell becomes and, more usefully, what
reading the local Next 16.3.4 docs changed about the plan.

Two hypotheses from the pre-flight died there. The contextual rail was
going to be a parallel route slot; the docs say a soft navigation keeps a
slot's last active subpage when the new route has no match, so the home's
rail would follow the reader into an empty section. Avoiding that needs a
null page per rail-less route, which is the guard-per-page antipattern
this repository refuses elsewhere. The rail is composed by the page.

The scroll model was going to be three overflow containers. The docs say
Next skips sticky and fixed elements when it looks for the scroll target,
so a sticky sidebar and a sticky rail leave the document as the axis --
which keeps browser scroll restoration, hash anchors and the mobile URL
bar for free.

React's ViewTransition turns out to need no configuration at all, and is
still declined this phase: it animates the whole document by default,
which is the one thing the shell must not do.

ADR-0028 records that the kanban geometry can be built before the domain
but the domain cannot be guessed from the geometry, that the client's
board is read-only because approval is a validated RPC and a drag cannot
express "request changes", and that @dnd-kit is the direction for phase
10 with nothing installed now.

